        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, drilling waste, 71.5% water, to landfarming</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, drilling waste, 71.5% water, to landfarming
Inventoried waste contains 100% drilling waste; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): upper heating value 0.773 MJ/kg; H2O 714700; O 100000; H 5000; C 30000; S 6000; N n.a.; P 500; B 100; Cl 35000; Br n.a.; F 500; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 4; Ba 5000; Cd n.a.; Co n.a.; Cr 50; Cu n.a.; Hg n.a.; Mn 400; Mo n.a.; Ni n.a.; Pb n.a.; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn 150; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr 100; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 1000; Fe 20000; Ca 40000; Al 10000; K 3500; Mg 8000; Na 20000; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%.; UUID: bfe6fa34-144b-455c-9ccf-c72cf0b3a497
direct emissions from landfarming applications (100% to industrial soil). Burden for spreading process.
Location: undefined
Technology: direct spreading on industrial areas. No crop growing.
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste compositions from literature data. 
Extrapolations: Spreading process approximated with vacuum tank spreader
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_bfe6fa34-144b-455c-9ccf-c72cf0b3a497.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
